<title>SINGAPORE: Component stocks in new Singapore regional index.</title>
<headline>Component stocks in new Singapore regional index.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stock Exchange of Singapore (SES) said on Tuesday the following 38 local and foreign firms would be included in its new share index for companies listed in Singapore with substantial operations across Asia.</p>
<p>The Business Times Singapore Regional Index (BT-SRI), which is weighted by market capitalisation, includes 24 stocks quoted in Singapore dollars and 14 in U.S. dollars. Seven of the components are the foreign tranches of Singapore firms with both local and foreign tranche listings.</p>
<p>In alphabetical order, the firms are:</p>
<p>Acer Computer International Ltd</p>
<p>Cerebos Pacific Ltd</p>
<p>Clipsal Industries Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Cycle &amp; Carriage Ltd</p>
<p>Dairy Farm International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Datacraft Asia Ltd</p>
<p>Development bank of Singapore Ltd</p>
<p>Elec &amp; Eltek International Co Ltd</p>
<p>Far East Levingston Shipbuilding Ltd</p>
<p>Fraser &amp; Neave Ltd</p>
<p>GP Batteries International Ltd</p>
<p>Guthrie GTS Ltd</p>
<p>Haw Par Brothers International Ltd</p>
<p>Hongkong Land Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Inchcape Berhad</p>
<p>Jardine Matheson Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Jardine Strategic Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Keppel Corp Ltd</p>
<p>Kim Eng Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Mandarin Oriental International Ltd</p>
<p>Natsteel Ltd</p>
<p>Neptune Orient Lines Ltd</p>
<p>Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp Ltd</p>
<p>Overseas Union Bank Ltd</p>
<p>Pacific Carriers Ltd</p>
<p>Roly International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>Sembawang Maritime Ltd</p>
<p>Shangri-La Hotel Ltd</p>
<p>Singapore Airlines Ltd</p>
<p>Singapore Petroleum Co Ltd</p>
<p>Singapore Telecommunications Ltd</p>
<p>Singmarine Industries Ltd</p>
<p>ST Shipbuilding &amp; Engineering Ltd</p>
<p>Thakral Corp Ltd</p>
<p>Total Access Communication Public Co Ltd</p>
<p>United Overseas Bank Ltd</p>
<p>Want Want Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>WBL Corp Ltd</p>
